  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nThe large Pacific upper low will slowly steer inland onto the\ncoasts of Washington/Oregon on Sunday and the low core will \npass directly over our area through Monday, returning moderate \nto widespread precipitation late Sunday into Monday. Guidance \ncontinues to track the low steering moisture from Hurricane \nMarie into the Upper Great Basin and near our area come Monday. \nThe moisture will remain close enough for south-central Idaho to\nexperience heightened chances for heavier rainfall, especially \nthe central mountains. Snow levels are still expected to drop \nlow enough over the highest peaks for a rain and snow mix, \nmainly on Monday.\n\nBelow-normal temperatures will persist through early next week\ndue to upper troughing and widespread cloud cover. Latest \nlong-range guidance suggests another Pacific upper low steering \ninto the region Tuesday through Thursday, but with considerable \nuncertainty over its magnitude and behavior towards late week. \nFor now, drier conditions and warmer temperatures are expected \nTuesday through late next week. The approaching low may return \nscattered precipitation on Thursday, depending on the amount of \nPacific moisture steered into our area.",
